{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/106434","id":2521589947,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6WTGi7","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106434","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106434.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106434.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106434","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/106434/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/106434/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106434/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/ad600125df2ce267e48fb1588d688b858647321c","number":106434,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Reduce cross project includes by rewriting `HashMapHasherDefault`.","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"- Helps address https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111218\r\n\r\nGodot is plagued by long compile times because of unnecessary cross project includes.\r\nTwo of the main culprits in Core are `hashfuncs.h` and `variant.h`.\r\nThis PR eliminates cross project includes from `hashfuncs.h`, to improve compile time and reduce type coupling.\r\n\r\n### Explanation\r\n\r\n`HashMapHasherDefault` was previously written by implementing a `static uint32_t hash(const T &)` function for every known `Variant` type. As `Variant` types grew, so did the includes for `hashfuncs.h`.\r\n\r\nI rewrote the struct by adding a type trait called `HashMapHasherDefaultImpl<T>`. This type trait can be declared for any type, providing a hash function for default hashing, analogous to `HashMapComparatorDefault`.\r\n\r\nThe type trait is specialized for primitives (like `double` and `int32_t`).\r\nIt is further specialized for `enum` types by using the underlying type, which was also the previous behavior (through implicit conversion). \r\n\r\nIt is also specialized for types that declare `uint32_t hash() const;`, by calling this function. This behavior was previously implemented with `HashableHasher`, whose implementation claimed it is only possible to generalize this with c++20 concepts. I removed the now unnecessary `HashableHasher` type.\r\nUsing this specialization, hash functions are moved to the appropriate types. By this move, the includes from `hashfuncs.h` could be removed.\r\n\r\nThe same trick was applied to `HashMapDefaultComparator`, which previously had unnecessary specializations that all called `is_same`. I generalized this assumption with type trait logic (SFINAE).\r\n\r\n### Side effects\r\n\r\n- `Color` was previously hashed by converting to `String` and hashing the string (through implicit conversion). This was slow. I optimized the conversion to hash with the components instead.\r\n- `hash_map` previously needed a `Variant` include because it declared a function that assumed `Variant` keys. I generalized the function to use a comparator, and moved the variant comparison method to `dictionary.cpp` (the only place where it was used). This allowed me to delete `hash_map.cpp`.\r\n- It is no longer possible to \"auto-declare\" hashing functions by declaring an implicit conversion operator. This is sane, especially since we have many lossy and slow implicit conversion operators in the codebase (as seen on `Color`). Two types now need to define an explicit hashing function that did not need to declare it before.\r\n-  It is now possible to hash `enum struct`, which was not possible before. Previously, the enum needed to be implicitly convertible to its underlying type, to support being hashed by `HashMapHasherDefault`.\r\n- I had a problem with `ImageLoaderSVG` remotely, to debug it I inserted the error code to the error message. It seems to have mysteriously disappeared, but I'd argue having the error code for the future is good anyway.\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097966,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTc5NjY=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:core","name":"topic:core","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098009,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgwMDk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:buildsystem","name":"topic:buildsystem","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2304948121,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyMzA0OTQ4MTIx","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:codestyle","name":"topic:codestyle","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":3240950060,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzMjQwOTUwMDYw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/performance","name":"performance","description":"","color":"447777","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":12939969,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AxXLB","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/23","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/23","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/23/labels","number":23,"state":"closed","title":"4.6","description":"","creator":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":3,"closed_issues":2978,"created_at":"2025-05-22T16:25:52Z","updated_at":"2026-10-04T16:23:23Z","closed_at":"2026-01-26T18:09:14Z","due_on":null},"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2025-05-15T10:02:08Z","updated_at":"2025-10-06T14:16:26Z","closed_at":"2025-10-06T14:13:04Z","merged_at":"2025-10-06T14:13:04Z","merge_commit_sha":"686b56fae9121c5ec4435b824e921db17389969b","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"Ivorforce:invert-hashfuncs","ref":"invert-hashfuncs","repo":{"id":861387944,"node_id":"R_kgDOM1e8qA","